{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T6f8BWy333dmJJH2Lkg5Ji","type":"tool_result","content":"400\t      # (\"do NOT re-list them as paths\").\n401\t      #\n402\t      # UNCONDITIONAL on purpose. The instrument ships in its own commit\n403\t      # (PLAN-185 W0, 7383518) and is a tracked file, so there is no checkout\n404\t      # of this workflow's own branch where it is legitimately absent. A\n405\t      # defensive `if [ -f … ]` was considered and REJECTED: it converts a\n406\t      # blocking gate into one that reports success when it ran nothing, which\n407\t      # is the exact class the negative control in smoke-install.yml exists to\n408\t      # prevent. If the instrument is ever missing, RED is the correct answer —\n409\t      # it means the bundle did not land.\n410\t      # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n411\t      - name: Run check-installer-write-safety.py (PLAN-185 W0)\n412\t        run: |\n413\t          set -euo pipefail\n414\t          python3 .claude/scripts/check-installer-write-safety.py\n415\t\n416\t      # ADVISORY, never a gate (PLAN-185 OQ-1). The ratchet above is blind to\n417\t      # ONE thing by design: the baseline waives `indeterminado`, so that set\n418\t      # can GROW without turning any check red. This step is that set's\n419\t      # readout — one line per PR, so the debt is visible while OQ-1 is open.\n420\t      # `continue-on-error: true` makes it structurally incapable of blocking\n421\t      # a merge. Output is BOUNDED on purpose: `--strict` lists every site\n422\t      # (424 lines today), which is a wall nobody reads, so only the summary\n423\t      # line and a short tail are printed. The rc is captured immediately and\n424\t      # printed rather than swallowed — `cmd > log; RC=$?` and never\n425\t      # `cmd || true`, which would report success for every outcome.\n426\t      - name: check-installer-write-safety.py --strict (advisory, OQ-1)\n427\t        continue-on-error: true\n428\t        run: |\n429\t          set -uo pipefail\n430\t          LOG=\"${RUNNER_TEMP:-/tmp}/iws-strict.log\"\n431\t          python3 .claude/scripts/check-installer-write-safety.py --strict > \"$LOG\" 2>&1\n432\t          RC=$?\n433\t          echo \"--strict rc=$RC — ADVISORY; OQ-1 decides when (and whether) this becomes a gate.\"\n434\t          grep -E '^--strict: ' \"$LOG\" || echo \"(no --strict summary line — see the tail below)\"\n435\t          tail -n 15 \"$LOG\"\n436\t\n437\t      # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n438\t      # Step: Python toolchain for the steps below (Sprint 2 A.4)\n439\t      # PLAN-186 W4a deleted the hook/script unit-test steps this banner\n440\t      # used to introduce; `hook-tests-python-matrix` runs those suites\n441\t      # now, in 3.9 AND 3.12. What stays is the toolchain later steps of\n442\t      # this job still use — MEASURED, not assumed: TWO of them INVOKE\n443\t      # pytest (the PLAN-155 Wave 6 teeth and the PLAN-152 tests-01\n444\t      # roots); the npm packlist gate uses the selected python3\n445\t      # interpreter but NOT pytest. So: Python 3.12 from setup-python\n446\t      # (audit-v2 hot-fix: the ubuntu-24.04 default python3 ships\n447\t      # without pytest) plus pytest itself.\n448\t      # PyYAML IS needed: since PLAN-194 W1.2 the YAML catalog step runs\n449\t      # right after the install below and imports it."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a75fce92-96ca-4d13-a29e-d655897f3e0a","uuid":"5c54e964-b5d4-402c-82eb-02cefbde71ad","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:55:45.180Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.github/workflows/validate.yml","content":"      # (\"do NOT re-list them as paths\").\n      #\n      # UNCONDITIONAL on purpose. The instrument ships in its own commit\n      # (PLAN-185 W0, 7383518) and is a tracked file, so there is no checkout\n      # of this workflow's own branch where it is legitimately absent. A\n      # defensive `if [ -f … ]` was considered and REJECTED: it converts a\n      # blocking gate into one that reports success when it ran nothing, which\n      # is the exact class the negative control in smoke-install.yml exists to\n      # prevent. If the instrument is ever missing, RED is the correct answer —\n      # it means the bundle did not land.\n      # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n      - name: Run check-installer-write-safety.py (PLAN-185 W0)\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          python3 .claude/scripts/check-installer-write-safety.py\n\n      # ADVISORY, never a gate (PLAN-185 OQ-1). The ratchet above is blind to\n      # ONE thing by design: the baseline waives `indeterminado`, so that set\n      # can GROW without turning any check red. This step is that set's\n      # readout — one line per PR, so the debt is visible while OQ-1 is open.\n      # `continue-on-error: true` makes it structurally incapable of blocking\n      # a merge. Output is BOUNDED on purpose: `--strict` lists every site\n      # (424 lines today), which is a wall nobody reads, so only the summary\n      # line and a short tail are printed. The rc is captured immediately and\n      # printed rather than swallowed — `cmd > log; RC=$?` and never\n      # `cmd || true`, which would report success for every outcome.\n      - name: check-installer-write-safety.py --strict (advisory, OQ-1)\n        continue-on-error: true\n        run: |\n          set -uo pipefail\n          LOG=\"${RUNNER_TEMP:-/tmp}/iws-strict.log\"\n          python3 .claude/scripts/check-installer-write-safety.py --strict > \"$LOG\" 2>&1\n          RC=$?\n          echo \"--strict rc=$RC — ADVISORY; OQ-1 decides when (and whether) this becomes a gate.\"\n          grep -E '^--strict: ' \"$LOG\" || echo \"(no --strict summary line — see the tail below)\"\n          tail -n 15 \"$LOG\"\n\n      # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n      # Step: Python toolchain for the steps below (Sprint 2 A.4)\n      # PLAN-186 W4a deleted the hook/script unit-test steps this banner\n      # used to introduce; `hook-tests-python-matrix` runs those suites\n      # now, in 3.9 AND 3.12. What stays is the toolchain later steps of\n      # this job still use — MEASURED, not assumed: TWO of them INVOKE\n      # pytest (the PLAN-155 Wave 6 teeth and the PLAN-152 tests-01\n      # roots); the npm packlist gate uses the selected python3\n      # interpreter but NOT pytest. So: Python 3.12 from setup-python\n      # (audit-v2 hot-fix: the ubuntu-24.04 default python3 ships\n      # without pytest) plus pytest itself.\n      # PyYAML IS needed: since PLAN-194 W1.2 the YAML catalog step runs\n      # right after the install below and imports it.","numLines":50,"startLine":400,"totalLines":1787}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T6f8BWy333dmJJH2Lkg5Ji","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
