{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MBDvbkwCXfp7kCpnbePN1H","type":"tool_result","content":"210\t    # requires CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE=PLAN-156-COUNCIL-GUARD-EXTENSION AND\n211\t    # CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT in addition to SENT-GK-F.\n212\t    #\n213\t    # PLAN-156-FOLLOWUP F3 (S270 live-fire finding, OQ1 Owner-ratified):\n214\t    # the exact-path entry guarded the INSTANCE, not the CLASS. A sibling\n215\t    # (or nested) workflow could carry the same external-lane egress and be\n216\t    # ordinary-writable — \"a file we choose not to ship is exactly the file\n217\t    # an attacker would CREATE\". The glob covers subdirectories too; `**`\n218\t    # matches zero or more segments in _fnmatch_segments (Sprint 9).\n219\t    # Cost accepted at ratification: authoring ANY .claude/workflows/*.js\n220\t    # becomes a sentinel ceremony.\n221\t    \".claude/workflows/**/*.js\",\n222\t    \".claude/commands/council.md\",\n223\t    # PLAN-165 p1-corrected (CX-1, S290): the night-mode posture-write\n224\t    # surface. The per-tool deny entries in settings.json close the\n225\t    # Edit/Write rail; THESE entries are the load-bearing rail for Bash —\n226\t    # check_bash_safety keys write-shaped (and -c/-e-body) command\n227\t    # references off this list, so without them\n228\t    # `echo '{...}' > settings.local.json` passes under acceptEdits with\n229\t    # the deny applied (the codex CX-1 refutation of the original p1).\n230\t    # Listing the WRITER script here also removes model-rail invocation\n231\t    # of the toggle (OQ1-redo, Owner-ratified 2026-08-03: presence =\n232\t    # only a human at the keyboard runs on/off, via `!` or a terminal).\n233\t    \".claude/settings.local.json\",\n234\t    \".claude/state/night-mode.json\",\n235\t    \".claude/scripts/night-mode.py\",\n236\t    # PLAN162_FIX_3 (PLAN-162 findings #3 + #8, consensus C10) — guard the\n237\t    # files the guard itself TRUSTS. Both were guarded by NEITHER rail on\n238\t    # HEAD (verified: canonical=False AND kernel=False), which is what\n239\t    # separates them from finding #12 (that one at least has the kernel\n240\t    # hard-deny underneath).\n241\t    #\n242\t    #   1. `.claude/security/sentinel-signers-registry.yaml` — the ADR-121\n243\t    #      identity root read below in `_sentinel_grants_path`. An ordinary\n244\t    #      Edit silently disarmed half the dual signer rail.\n245\t    #   2. `.claude/policies/.drift-manifest.json` — the policy hash-pin\n246\t    #      registry. Rewritable without the sentinel it pins; the parallel\n247\t    #      of #3 (\"pin the pinner\").\n248\t    #\n249\t    # BOTH are ALSO in `_KERNEL_PATHS` (same wave) — the sentinel rail"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a75fce92-96ca-4d13-a29e-d655897f3e0a","uuid":"268a20c1-be73-47ef-8da4-4cc62c934dc9","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:57:12.167Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/guards.py","content":"    # requires CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE=PLAN-156-COUNCIL-GUARD-EXTENSION AND\n    # CEO_KERNEL_OVERRIDE_ACK=I-ACCEPT in addition to SENT-GK-F.\n    #\n    # PLAN-156-FOLLOWUP F3 (S270 live-fire finding, OQ1 Owner-ratified):\n    # the exact-path entry guarded the INSTANCE, not the CLASS. A sibling\n    # (or nested) workflow could carry the same external-lane egress and be\n    # ordinary-writable — \"a file we choose not to ship is exactly the file\n    # an attacker would CREATE\". The glob covers subdirectories too; `**`\n    # matches zero or more segments in _fnmatch_segments (Sprint 9).\n    # Cost accepted at ratification: authoring ANY .claude/workflows/*.js\n    # becomes a sentinel ceremony.\n    \".claude/workflows/**/*.js\",\n    \".claude/commands/council.md\",\n    # PLAN-165 p1-corrected (CX-1, S290): the night-mode posture-write\n    # surface. The per-tool deny entries in settings.json close the\n    # Edit/Write rail; THESE entries are the load-bearing rail for Bash —\n    # check_bash_safety keys write-shaped (and -c/-e-body) command\n    # references off this list, so without them\n    # `echo '{...}' > settings.local.json` passes under acceptEdits with\n    # the deny applied (the codex CX-1 refutation of the original p1).\n    # Listing the WRITER script here also removes model-rail invocation\n    # of the toggle (OQ1-redo, Owner-ratified 2026-08-03: presence =\n    # only a human at the keyboard runs on/off, via `!` or a terminal).\n    \".claude/settings.local.json\",\n    \".claude/state/night-mode.json\",\n    \".claude/scripts/night-mode.py\",\n    # PLAN162_FIX_3 (PLAN-162 findings #3 + #8, consensus C10) — guard the\n    # files the guard itself TRUSTS. Both were guarded by NEITHER rail on\n    # HEAD (verified: canonical=False AND kernel=False), which is what\n    # separates them from finding #12 (that one at least has the kernel\n    # hard-deny underneath).\n    #\n    #   1. `.claude/security/sentinel-signers-registry.yaml` — the ADR-121\n    #      identity root read below in `_sentinel_grants_path`. An ordinary\n    #      Edit silently disarmed half the dual signer rail.\n    #   2. `.claude/policies/.drift-manifest.json` — the policy hash-pin\n    #      registry. Rewritable without the sentinel it pins; the parallel\n    #      of #3 (\"pin the pinner\").\n    #\n    # BOTH are ALSO in `_KERNEL_PATHS` (same wave) — the sentinel rail","numLines":40,"startLine":210,"totalLines":387}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MBDvbkwCXfp7kCpnbePN1H","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
